              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="4">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Builds a design-storm hyetograph from an IDF (Intensity-Duration-Frequency) curve, with an optional climate allowance. Feed it to Stormwater Run.

Give it EITHER the three coefficients of an i = a/(t+b)^c fit, OR a published depth-duration table (the form NOAA Atlas 14, KOSTRA and FEH actually distribute). The alternating-block and Chicago patterns reproduce the IDF depth at every sub-duration, which is what makes the result a design event rather than a shape.

Version 1.8.0.827

Version 1.8.0.827

Version 1.12.0.827

Version 1.15.0.827</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">461868e8-7924-4bb0-82cc-793e4b1435a6</item>
