                    <chunk name="param_input" index="1">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Raster cell size in metres. 1–5 m compares options across a catchment; 0.25–0.5 m is needed only when a sub-metre feature itself drives the answer — and before reaching for it, try burning that feature in as a Breakline, which is far cheaper and, on the repository's own test case, recovers the retention a fine raster resolves to within about 7%.</item>
