                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Kerbs, swale inverts, thresholds and low walls, as curves. Each is burned along the cells it crosses so it survives a coarse grid.

The Breakline Offsets input says what each does: a positive value raises the ground by that much (a 150 mm kerb is 0.15), a negative value cuts a swale, and 0 sets the ground to the curve's own z.</item>
